      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the anxiety thing but this is different. it's not just seeing things i didn't post, it's that the 'me' on there knows things about my childhood that i never even put online. like specific details about a private conversation i had with my dad ten years ago. if it's just an algorithm, how does it have access to my private memories? it feels like they've actually mapped my mind. if you won't help me look for the discrepancies, at least tell me how a system like that would actually function so i can see if what i'm seeing fits the pattern.",
